WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.041 --> 00:00:00.792
Abe, the

00:00:00.792 --> 00:00:02.711
UAW member, excuse me,

00:00:02.711 --> 00:00:04.879
are now officially on strike.

00:00:04.879 --> 00:00:06.548
You can hear the horns right now.

00:00:06.548 --> 00:00:08.383
You are there in Wayne, Michigan,

00:00:08.383 --> 00:00:09.384
where the UAW

00:00:09.384 --> 00:00:10.844
president John Thain

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:11.678
and other members

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:13.430
are already on the picket line.

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:14.514
What is the mood

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:16.474
like where you are right now?

00:00:16.474 --> 00:00:18.727
This is very significant.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.106
It is its history.

00:00:23.106 --> 00:00:24.065
It's the first time we have seen

00:00:24.065 --> 00:00:25.358
this simultaneous strike

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:27.235
against the big three automakers

00:00:27.235 --> 00:00:28.278
in the United States

00:00:28.278 --> 00:00:29.863
where outside a Ford plant right now.

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:31.364
And you can probably hear that energy.

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:33.366
It has been a bit chaotic here

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:34.159
the last few minutes.

00:00:34.159 --> 00:00:35.368
Hundreds of people

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:36.161
flowing in

00:00:36.161 --> 00:00:38.413
to be on this initial strike line.

00:00:38.413 --> 00:00:39.330
You can see it behind me.

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:41.291
This is history playing out.

00:00:41.291 --> 00:00:42.042
Now I want to bring in

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:43.793
it was Ashley, is that right?

00:00:43.793 --> 00:00:45.628
Amanda excuse me, Amanda Sinclair.

00:00:45.628 --> 00:00:46.046
Amanda.

00:00:47.422 --> 00:00:49.299
Amanda, you work on the box line.

00:00:49.299 --> 00:00:51.342
You said that, right? Yes.

00:00:51.342 --> 00:00:51.718
Okay.

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:53.762
So you are now on strike

00:00:53.762 --> 00:00:55.513
along with about 3000

00:00:55.513 --> 00:00:56.264
other people

00:00:56.264 --> 00:00:58.183
who work here at the factory.

00:00:58.183 --> 00:00:59.684
Tell me how you're feeling tonight.

00:00:59.684 --> 00:01:00.769
I feel it's worth

00:01:00.769 --> 00:01:01.728
being out here on strike

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.396
because we need more money.

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:05.023
Like the cost of living. It went up.

00:01:05.023 --> 00:01:06.691
So that's why I'm out here.

00:01:06.691 --> 00:01:07.567
I just got off work,

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:08.985
and I came out here to strike.

00:01:08.985 --> 00:01:09.611
You were working

00:01:09.611 --> 00:01:11.071
until just a few minutes ago.

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:12.489
Yeah, you know.

00:01:12.489 --> 00:01:13.490
And what to you

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:15.408
in this negotiation is most important.

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:16.493
What are you looking for?

00:01:16.493 --> 00:01:18.787
You cost the living more money.

00:01:19.871 --> 00:01:22.540
No, we have everything that we ask for

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:24.250
as of tomorrow.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.752
It seems you're going to be on a

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:26.628
strike pay.

00:01:26.628 --> 00:01:27.670
Is that your understanding?

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:29.047
Making about $100 a day?

00:01:29.047 --> 00:01:31.091
Yeah. That's not enough at all. Yeah.

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:32.509
How are you going to get by?

00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:34.219
And how long are you ready to be

00:01:34.219 --> 00:01:36.096
on that picket line? Fighting.

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.972
Making only $100 a day.

00:01:37.972 --> 00:01:39.224
I don't know how I survive,

00:01:39.224 --> 00:01:39.974
but I'm going to do it.

00:01:39.974 --> 00:01:41.101
I'm a B, I hear here striking.

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:43.103
Well, thank you so much

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:44.771
for your time, Amanda. Appreciate it.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:45.271
And again,

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:46.731
if you look behind me, Laura,

00:01:46.731 --> 00:01:48.858
this is what history looks like.

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.443
Hundreds of people we know

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:52.904
there are 3000 members

00:01:52.904 --> 00:01:53.863
who are going to be striking

00:01:53.863 --> 00:01:55.907
at this location, just one of three.

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:57.992
There's also a GM plant

00:01:58.118 --> 00:01:59.661
in Waynesville, Missouri,

00:01:59.661 --> 00:02:02.622
and a Stellantis plant in Toledo, Ohio,

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:05.667
between the three, about 13,000 members.

00:02:05.708 --> 00:02:06.543
The question

00:02:06.543 --> 00:02:07.669
is, Laura,

00:02:07.669 --> 00:02:09.212
how much of a disruption

00:02:09.212 --> 00:02:10.463
is that going to cause

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:11.172
to the auto

00:02:11.172 --> 00:02:12.924
manufacturing industry

00:02:12.924 --> 00:02:14.259
here in the United States?

00:02:14.259 --> 00:02:15.885
Because obviously,

00:02:15.885 --> 00:02:17.679
when cars can't be finished,

00:02:17.679 --> 00:02:18.972
if certain parts can't be made,

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:20.932
it could shut the whole process down

00:02:20.932 --> 00:02:22.016
across the country.

00:02:22.016 --> 00:02:23.309
There's concern about that

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:24.853
and about the economic impacts.

00:02:24.853 --> 00:02:26.312
But that's not what tonight is about.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:27.063
As you can hear.

00:02:28.022 --> 00:02:28.565
You can hear the

00:02:28.565 --> 00:02:30.900
energy people who are excited

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:33.987
and it seems like they are ready for this

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:35.738
to potentially last a while.

00:02:35.738 --> 00:02:37.657
How long is a mystery?

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:39.033
It just started about,

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:40.910
as you know, 2 minutes ago.

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:41.619
I mean, just thinking

00:02:41.619 --> 00:02:42.745
about the significance

00:02:42.745 --> 00:02:43.371
when you just spoke

00:02:43.371 --> 00:02:45.415
to coming off of work

00:02:45.415 --> 00:02:46.207
prepared now

00:02:46.207 --> 00:02:47.584
to strike waiting,

00:02:47.584 --> 00:02:48.042
she says

00:02:48.042 --> 00:02:49.752
perhaps as long as it would take to get

00:02:49.752 --> 00:02:51.796
what is owed to them in belief,

00:02:51.796 --> 00:02:53.047
using the phrase that it seems

00:02:53.047 --> 00:02:54.716
to be worth it to do so.

00:02:54.716 --> 00:02:56.217
13,000 members

00:02:56.217 --> 00:02:57.969
I mean, there are these three locations

00:02:57.969 --> 00:02:59.470
now across the country.

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:01.556
Are the major automakers game

00:03:01.556 --> 00:03:03.016
saying anything tonight

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:06.477
about now where we are on strike

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:09.606
Well, look, we've

00:03:09.606 --> 00:03:11.858
heard from the president of Ford today.

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:13.401
We know there has been frustration

00:03:13.401 --> 00:03:14.444
from these automakers

00:03:14.444 --> 00:03:14.986
who feel like

00:03:14.986 --> 00:03:16.321
the union

00:03:16.446 --> 00:03:17.113
has waited,

00:03:17.113 --> 00:03:18.907
has not negotiated in good faith

00:03:18.907 --> 00:03:20.241
that they have offered

00:03:20.241 --> 00:03:22.744
large pay increases up to 20%.

00:03:22.785 --> 00:03:24.829
We know the union is seeking 40%,

00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:25.872
but it seems like

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:27.999
there is still a wide gap between them.

00:03:27.999 --> 00:03:30.001
Listening to these car companies

00:03:30.001 --> 00:03:31.002
talk tonight

00:03:31.002 --> 00:03:31.836
and basically say

00:03:31.836 --> 00:03:33.046
they have come to the table.

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:34.172
But as of now,

00:03:34.172 --> 00:03:34.505
there is

00:03:34.505 --> 00:03:36.466
seems to have been little progress.

00:03:36.466 --> 00:03:37.383
Laura.

00:03:37.508 --> 00:03:38.301
I mean, they're talking a lot

00:03:38.301 --> 00:03:39.469
about these tiers, people

00:03:39.469 --> 00:03:40.595
who are being working

00:03:40.595 --> 00:03:41.763
in the same positions,

00:03:41.763 --> 00:03:43.056
getting paid at different amounts,

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:44.265
hoping to end that.

00:03:44.265 --> 00:03:44.682
Of course,

00:03:44.682 --> 00:03:45.725
just looking at the energy

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:48.186
behind you game since you've arrived,

00:03:48.186 --> 00:03:49.103
it has increased

00:03:49.103 --> 00:03:50.230
almost exponentially

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:52.065
in the size of the crowd behind you.

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:54.108
Drivers going by honking,

00:03:54.108 --> 00:03:55.151
likely in support

00:03:55.151 --> 00:03:56.903
of what is happening right now.

00:03:56.903 --> 00:03:57.779
And by the way,

00:03:57.779 --> 00:03:58.154
we did

00:03:58.154 --> 00:03:59.948
invite the three executives

00:03:59.948 --> 00:04:02.408
from all three of the auto companies.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:05.161
They have declined to join us tonight.

00:04:05.453 --> 00:04:06.496
We're going to keep checking back

00:04:06.496 --> 00:04:07.330
with you.

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:08.915
Stay there and keep us informed

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:10.625
about what's happening on the ground.

00:04:10.625 --> 00:04:11.084
Joining me

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:13.836
now is Congresswoman Haley Stevens,

00:04:13.836 --> 00:04:15.129
a Michigan Democrat

00:04:15.129 --> 00:04:16.881
who supports the strikers

00:04:16.881 --> 00:04:18.216
Congresswoman Stevens,

00:04:18.216 --> 00:04:20.134
they are officially on strike.

00:04:20.134 --> 00:04:21.886
It happened moments ago.

00:04:21.886 --> 00:04:22.720
It is historic.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:24.889
And you are standing in solidarity

00:04:24.889 --> 00:04:26.891
with the UAW members

00:04:26.891 --> 00:04:29.310
How significant is this strike?

00:04:30.311 --> 00:04:31.688
Well, you've got that right.

00:04:31.688 --> 00:04:34.357
I'm absolutely standing alongside

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:35.108
the hard

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:37.110
working men and women of the UAW.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.111
And I want to thank Gabe

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:41.322
for being out with the workers striking,

00:04:41.322 --> 00:04:41.948
I think a man.

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:44.534
This story is incredibly significant,

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:46.869
a woman who just got off her shift

00:04:46.869 --> 00:04:47.245
and who's

00:04:47.245 --> 00:04:49.372
now joined the picket line saying

00:04:49.747 --> 00:04:51.749
I want a better deal.

00:04:51.749 --> 00:04:53.209
And the American people

00:04:53.209 --> 00:04:54.419
have to understand,

00:04:54.419 --> 00:04:56.254
it's not easy to strike.

00:04:56.254 --> 00:04:58.214
It is nerve wracking.

00:04:58.214 --> 00:05:00.216
A lot is put on the line.

00:05:00.216 --> 00:05:01.676
But the outcome of this

00:05:01.676 --> 00:05:03.428
has got to be a better deal

00:05:03.428 --> 00:05:04.554
for the workers.

00:05:04.554 --> 00:05:06.264
And that's what we're seeing play out.

00:05:06.264 --> 00:05:08.349
That's why we're in this position.

00:05:08.349 --> 00:05:09.726
And I'm going to be standing

00:05:09.726 --> 00:05:11.769
by the UAW through and through.

00:05:11.769 --> 00:05:13.062
I mean, just the anxiety in you.

00:05:13.062 --> 00:05:13.730
And I'm so glad

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:14.856
that you mentioned the

00:05:14.856 --> 00:05:16.232
human element of this

00:05:16.232 --> 00:05:17.066
as we're talking a lot

00:05:17.066 --> 00:05:18.735
about manufacturing,

00:05:18.735 --> 00:05:19.360
where it's going to be

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:21.487
in terms of the economy and areas around

00:05:22.071 --> 00:05:24.198
what how will impact the big three

00:05:24.615 --> 00:05:27.035
for every person who is on this line?

00:05:27.076 --> 00:05:27.660
Every person

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.329
contemplating whether to strike

00:05:29.329 --> 00:05:30.455
has to consider

00:05:30.455 --> 00:05:31.873
exactly what you're talking about,

00:05:31.873 --> 00:05:34.208
what it will mean to them immediately

00:05:34.208 --> 00:05:35.752
over the next days or weeks.

00:05:35.752 --> 00:05:37.086
Perhaps even months ahead

00:05:37.086 --> 00:05:38.046
and what it was like over

00:05:38.046 --> 00:05:39.255
the next four years.

00:05:39.255 --> 00:05:39.964
Thank you for bringing

00:05:39.964 --> 00:05:41.591
that to our attention and reminding us.

00:05:41.591 --> 00:05:42.675
Congresswoman,

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:45.428
also, though, among the UAW demands

00:05:45.428 --> 00:05:47.847
is a 40% pay increase

00:05:48.139 --> 00:05:49.807
over a four year period.

00:05:49.807 --> 00:05:51.517
It also includes the restoration

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:52.018
of cost

00:05:52.018 --> 00:05:55.646
of living pay, raises a 32 hour work

00:05:55.897 --> 00:05:57.940
with 40 hours of pay.

00:05:57.940 --> 00:05:59.942
Are these fair asks?

00:06:01.319 --> 00:06:02.653
Well, I'm certainly not

00:06:02.653 --> 00:06:04.572
in the negotiating board room,

00:06:04.572 --> 00:06:06.783
but I think it's very fair

00:06:06.783 --> 00:06:09.994
for the workers to ask for their fair

00:06:09.994 --> 00:06:10.411
share.

00:06:10.411 --> 00:06:12.372
And I want to be crystal

00:06:12.372 --> 00:06:13.664
clear about what's taking place

00:06:13.664 --> 00:06:14.374
right now.

00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:16.000
Three plants

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.627
between the big three in three

00:06:17.627 --> 00:06:19.712
different states are on strike.

00:06:20.254 --> 00:06:21.547
There is oftentimes

00:06:21.547 --> 00:06:25.093
no question from large automakers

00:06:25.093 --> 00:06:27.303
when they decide to permanently

00:06:27.303 --> 00:06:28.388
close plants.

00:06:28.388 --> 00:06:28.971
We've seen

00:06:28.971 --> 00:06:32.350
that happen in droves over the last ten,

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:33.393
15 years.

00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:35.395
Dozens of plants shutting down.

00:06:35.395 --> 00:06:36.729
This is continued to happen

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:38.231
in the industrial Midwest

00:06:38.231 --> 00:06:40.691
while record profits

00:06:40.691 --> 00:06:43.444
are received by the large companies.

00:06:43.486 --> 00:06:46.531
And I'm proud of Michigan manufacturers.

00:06:46.531 --> 00:06:48.324
I'm so proud of the moment we're in.

00:06:48.324 --> 00:06:49.325
We were the ones

00:06:49.325 --> 00:06:49.867
who rose

00:06:49.867 --> 00:06:51.911
to the industrial call to action

00:06:51.911 --> 00:06:53.871
during the pandemic.

00:06:53.871 --> 00:06:56.040
We've continued to grow in industry

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:58.543
out of it and manage bankruptcy

00:06:59.085 --> 00:07:00.420
that I worked on in President

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:01.712
Obama's administration.

00:07:01.712 --> 00:07:03.297
I saw the UAW

00:07:03.297 --> 00:07:04.799
make concessions

00:07:04.799 --> 00:07:06.801
alongside many stakeholders.

00:07:07.093 --> 00:07:09.220
And now it's time to get fair share.

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:10.930
A strike is painful,

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:12.014
but the outcome

00:07:12.014 --> 00:07:13.141
and the long term

00:07:13.141 --> 00:07:14.475
benefits of this

00:07:14.475 --> 00:07:15.643
not just for the workers

00:07:15.643 --> 00:07:17.061
but for our economy

00:07:17.061 --> 00:07:19.522
as a whole, are on the horizon.

00:07:20.189 --> 00:07:21.190
Really important

00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:23.526
also that the Ford CEO, Jim Farley,

00:07:23.901 --> 00:07:24.610
spoke earlier

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:26.863
and talked about a 40% pay raise, saying

00:07:26.863 --> 00:07:28.781
that a 40% pay raise

00:07:28.781 --> 00:07:30.825
would actually bankrupt his company.

00:07:31.367 --> 00:07:33.035
Of course, a common retort

00:07:33.035 --> 00:07:33.703
to that is, well,

00:07:33.703 --> 00:07:34.745
what about the pay raises?

00:07:34.745 --> 00:07:35.746
People like yourself

00:07:35.746 --> 00:07:37.957
and your position would actually get?

00:07:37.957 --> 00:07:39.542
What's your reaction to his comment

00:07:39.542 --> 00:07:41.711
that this could potentially bankrupt this

00:07:41.711 --> 00:07:43.087
these industries?

00:07:43.296 --> 00:07:46.090
Well, Ford has made billions of dollars,

00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:47.341
tens of billions of dollars

00:07:47.341 --> 00:07:48.426
in just the first six months

00:07:48.426 --> 00:07:49.093
of this year.

00:07:49.093 --> 00:07:51.554
So I somewhat question

00:07:51.888 --> 00:07:54.223
the bankruptcy consideration,

00:07:54.223 --> 00:07:55.808
but certainly we

00:07:55.808 --> 00:07:57.727
we want to have a Ford Motor Company.

00:07:57.727 --> 00:07:59.145
We will continue to have a Ford

00:07:59.145 --> 00:08:00.521
Motor Company.

00:08:00.521 --> 00:08:03.399
And I encourage everyone to continue

00:08:03.441 --> 00:08:05.610
to negotiate in good faith.

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:07.820
We're seeing some signs of progress

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:08.946
when we hear

00:08:08.946 --> 00:08:10.698
that the companies are willing

00:08:10.698 --> 00:08:12.867
to meet on increased wages.

00:08:12.867 --> 00:08:14.702
But the tears that the

00:08:14.702 --> 00:08:16.078
the tier system

00:08:16.078 --> 00:08:18.372
that the UAW is asking for.

00:08:18.789 --> 00:08:19.916
Certainly COLA

00:08:19.916 --> 00:08:21.792
bringing COLA back, which was

00:08:22.752 --> 00:08:23.920
got a

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:27.131
negotiated as off the table 14 years ago.

00:08:27.548 --> 00:08:30.009
We'd like to see that come back in.

00:08:30.009 --> 00:08:32.178
And again, I'm not negotiating this deal,

00:08:32.428 --> 00:08:34.680
but I am standing by the UAW

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.307
and I think people should listen to Mr.

00:08:36.307 --> 00:08:37.391
Van right now

00:08:37.391 --> 00:08:38.684
and what he's pushing forward,

00:08:38.684 --> 00:08:39.602
see him

00:08:39.602 --> 00:08:41.562
with the UAW workers

00:08:41.562 --> 00:08:43.147
who are shaking his hand,

00:08:43.147 --> 00:08:44.982
who are appreciating someone

00:08:44.982 --> 00:08:48.861
who's of the UAW working alongside

00:08:49.237 --> 00:08:50.696
his brothers and sisters

00:08:50.696 --> 00:08:52.657
and not just shaking hands

00:08:52.657 --> 00:08:55.868
with politicians or other VIPs.

00:08:56.202 --> 00:08:57.036
He's doing this

